AetherSDR's 3D stacked-trace view ("3DSS"; https://github.com/ten9876/AetherSDR,
GPL-3.0), copied from the operator's fork ~/aether-orion at f7b405e2.

Unchanged but for the three-line header:
  DssRenderer.h/.cpp     the row store: peak-preserving resample to 768
                         columns, median-of-3 + 1-2-1 + 60/40 temporal
                         smoothing, per-row frequency frames, the shared
                         perspective constants, and a CPU image fallback
                         (unused here: the console's 3D is GPU only)
  DssDcEdgeMath.h        Flex-only (a DC-start spike); kept for their test
  ../shaders/dss_mesh.*  the GPU mesh shaders (one comment line added)
  tests/dsstest.cpp      their tests/dss_renderer_test.cpp (include paths)

Ported by hand from their SpectrumWidget.cpp into PanGpuView /
PanadapterWidget: the mesh pipeline + static mesh, the RGBA16F height ring
upload, the UBO packing, the back-to-front
draw with OpenGL's shared fill/outline pipeline, the slice-shadow decals
(VFO A/B passbands, "3D passband shading"), the floor anchor, the
"3D Gain" palette LUT and the Floor / Gain / Span controls.
